-- CONTROL: flips exactly ONE dimension — the two interfaces' METHOD NAMES are
-- distinct (`m` vs `mz`), so the method-keyed candidate set cannot mix the two
-- classes. Everything else is byte-for-byte the shape of main.mdk: same two
-- same-spelled `Same` interfaces, same shared head `Box a`, same `requires Eq a`
-- on one of them, same `Opaque` payload with no `Eq`.
--
-- Per #1144 this harness grades a control on its EXIT CODE ONLY, so this control
-- ASSERTS the correct value and panics otherwise rather than printing it — a
-- control that merely printed would exit 0 either way and could never fail.
-- Proven able to fail: change the comparand to a value the program cannot
-- produce and `medaka run control.mdk` exits 1 with `runtime error [E-PANIC]`.
import shared.{Box(..), Opaque(..)}
import cmod
import ymod.{useItZ}

main =
  let got = useItZ (Box Opaque)
  if got == 1 then
    println "control-ok:1"
  else
    panic "control expected 1, got \{intToString got}"
